# UPGRADE-05 — Production Release Hardening, Full Test Recovery,
# Anthropic Drift Guard & Reproducible Release

You are working directly inside the current ZCoder repository after
Upgrade-04 / v1.40.0 Truth Audit.

MISSION

Turn the truth-audited repository into a reproducible, production-grade
release that cannot pass while tests are ignored, Anthropic source data
is stale, version metadata is inconsistent, packaging is broken, or
critical CLI/API wiring is untested.

Do NOT begin by adding unrelated features.

Priority order:

P0 — Full test-suite recovery
P0 — Release/version integrity
P0 — Packaging/build/install verification
P0 — Anthropic conformance automation
P1 — CI matrix + release gates
P1 — runtime/transport contract testing
P1 — model/capability drift detection
P1 — CLI/web/TUI integration verification
P2 — observability, performance, DX hardening

Use first-party Anthropic sources only for Anthropic facts.

============================================================
1. BASELINE — DO NOT MODIFY CODE YET
============================================================

Record:

git status --short
git log -20 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -20

python --version

python -m pytest -q
python main.py --help

git diff --check

Also inspect:

pyproject.toml
setup.py
setup.cfg
requirements*.txt
tox.ini
pytest.ini
.github/workflows/
Dockerfile*
Makefile
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
anthropic-conformance.yaml

Determine whether v1.40.0 already exists as:

- git tag
- GitHub release
- package version
- PyPI release
- wheel/sdist artifact
- Docker image tag

DO NOT mutate or recreate an already-published immutable release.

============================================================
2. P0 — REMOVE THE IGNORED TEST EXCEPTION
============================================================

Upgrade-04 reported:

python3 -m pytest -q --tb=short --ignore=tests/test_webapp_server.py

This is NOT sufficient evidence of a complete production test suite.

Investigate:

tests/test_webapp_server.py

Determine exactly why it was excluded.

Classify failures as:

- application defect
- test defect
- missing optional dependency
- environment dependency
- port conflict
- event-loop issue
- race condition
- stale test
- unsupported platform
- packaging/import issue

Fix the root cause.

DO NOT:

- permanently ignore the test
- delete the test
- weaken assertions without evidence
- mark it xfail merely to obtain green CI
- catch all exceptions
- add arbitrary sleeps

If the functionality is genuinely optional, restructure the test suite:

tests/
  unit/
  integration/
  optional/
  contract/

and define explicit pytest markers such as:

@pytest.mark.integration
@pytest.mark.optional

The standard release suite must clearly state what it executes.

Required target:

python -m pytest -q

without --ignore.

If an external integration truly cannot run offline, its behavior must be
mocked at the transport boundary.

============================================================
3. TEST COUNT TRUTHFULNESS
============================================================

Do not report:

"100% tests passing"

when tests were skipped or excluded.

Instead report exact values:

PASSED
FAILED
SKIPPED
XFAILED
XFAILED-STRICT
DESELECTED

Create release-gate logic that fails if unexpected:

- ignored files
- deselected release tests
- xpass
- collection errors

A release result should distinguish:

TESTS_GREEN
OPTIONAL_TESTS_SKIPPED
TESTS_EXCLUDED

TESTS_EXCLUDED must prevent production release unless explicitly
approved by release policy.

============================================================
4. VERSION IMMUTABILITY / SEMVER AUDIT
============================================================

Upgrade-04 made corrective changes while still calling the result:

v1.40.0

Determine whether v1.40.0 was already published or tagged BEFORE those
changes.

If yes:

DO NOT rewrite v1.40.0.

Create a corrective release:

v1.40.1

unless additional backward-compatible features justify v1.41.0.

If v1.40.0 was never published/tagged and Upgrade-04 merely prepared the
release candidate, keeping v1.40.0 may be acceptable.

Prove the decision using repository state.

Synchronize the selected version across every source:

- pyproject.toml
- package __version__
- main.py
- CLI --version
- README
- CHANGELOG
- docs
- conformance manifest
- Docker labels
- package metadata
- release workflow

Add:

python main.py --version

and a test ensuring all version sources agree.

Prefer ONE canonical package version source.

============================================================
5. BUILD A REAL RELEASE ARTIFACT
============================================================

Verify package building.

Run, where appropriate:

python -m build

Validate:

dist/*.whl
dist/*.tar.gz

Then create a clean temporary environment and install the wheel:

python -m venv /tmp/zcoder-release-test
source /tmp/zcoder-release-test/bin/activate
pip install dist/*.whl

Test installed package behavior, not repository imports:

zcoder --version
zcoder --help

or the project's actual console command.

Run smoke tests from a directory OUTSIDE the repository so local source
files cannot mask missing package files.

Detect:

- undeclared dependencies
- missing package_data
- missing templates
- missing static assets
- accidental test dependencies
- editable-install assumptions
- import path leaks

============================================================
6. SDIST REPRODUCIBILITY
============================================================

Install and smoke-test the source distribution independently.

Check that:

wheel build
sdist build

contain equivalent required runtime assets.

Inspect artifact contents.

Prevent accidental packaging of:

- .env
- API keys
- credentials
- private audit dumps
- local logs
- caches
- build directories
- test secrets

============================================================
7. ANTHROPIC SOURCE-OF-TRUTH FETCHER
============================================================

Upgrade-04 created:

anthropic-conformance.yaml

Now make the conformance system operational.

Create a dedicated module such as:

anthropic_conformance.py

or an appropriate package location.

It must support:

zcoder anthropic conformance check

or an equivalent coherent command.

Responsibilities:

1. read the local conformance manifest
2. validate schema
3. determine last verification time
4. report source age
5. compare code registry against manifest
6. detect obvious contradictions
7. optionally perform LIVE source checks

Normal ZCoder startup MUST NOT require internet access.

Conformance checking must be explicit.

============================================================
8. SOURCE FRESHNESS POLICY
============================================================

Define freshness without pretending documentation dates are immutable.

Example status:

FRESH
STALE
UNKNOWN
OFFLINE

Track independently:

release_notes_checked_at
models_checked_at
pricing_checked_at
deprecations_checked_at
sdk_checked_at
claude_code_checked_at

Do not use a single global date.

Example:

source:
  name: anthropic_pricing
  url: ...
  checked_at: ...
  content_fingerprint: ...
  parser_version: ...

Do not claim a page was "updated" merely because it was fetched today.

============================================================
9. RELEASE-NOTE WATERMARK
============================================================

Persist the newest Anthropic Platform release-note DATE and feature IDs
seen during a successful audit.

At release time:

if upstream contains a newer release-note entry than the manifest
watermark:

SOURCE_TRUTH_PASS = false

until every new item has a disposition.

Allowed dispositions:

IMPLEMENTED_VERIFIED
IMPLEMENTED_NOT_APPLICABLE_TO_RUNTIME
MISSING
PARTIAL
DEPRECATED
RETIRED
CONSOLE_ONLY
ENTERPRISE_ONLY
PRIVATE_PREVIEW
RESEARCH_PREVIEW
DOCUMENTATION_ONLY

MISSING or PARTIAL P0/P1 items fail the gate.

============================================================
10. ANTHROPIC MODELS API LIVE VALIDATION
============================================================

Anthropic documentation states that the Models API exposes current model
metadata including capabilities and token limits.

Implement an OPTIONAL live conformance test using the authenticated
Models API.

It must NEVER be required for offline unit tests.

Example:

zcoder anthropic conformance models --live

Compare upstream results against the static/local registry.

Detect:

UNKNOWN_UPSTREAM_MODEL
LOCAL_MODEL_MISSING_UPSTREAM
CAPABILITY_DRIFT
TOKEN_LIMIT_DRIFT
MODEL_RETIRED
MODEL_NEWLY_AVAILABLE

Never automatically modify production code based on an API response.

Produce a proposed diff/report instead.

============================================================
11. STATIC MODEL REGISTRY VS LIVE DATA
============================================================

Separate:

STATIC_POLICY

from:

DISCOVERED_RUNTIME_METADATA

Static policy includes things Anthropic's Models API may not expose,
such as:

- application-specific routing policy
- pricing rules
- feature beta requirements
- known migration constraints

Live metadata includes only fields actually returned by Anthropic.

Never invent absent fields.

============================================================
12. PRICING DRIFT GUARD
============================================================

Upgrade-04 corrected Claude Sonnet 5 to:

$2 / MTok input
$10 / MTok output

Protect this class of bug permanently.

Pricing data should include:

model_id
platform
input_per_mtok
output_per_mtok
cache_5m_write
cache_1h_write
cache_read
batch_input
batch_output
effective_from
effective_until
verified_at
source

Do not implement a brittle HTML scraper as runtime infrastructure.

If automated documentation parsing is unreliable, use:

curated manifest + source fingerprint + human-reviewed update

rather than silently overwriting pricing.

============================================================
13. REQUEST/RESPONSE METADATA CONTRACT
============================================================

Upgrade-04 added response extraction in resilience.py.

Now ensure this is a first-class abstraction.

Create/normalize something similar to:

ResponseMetadata:
    request_id
    workspace_id
    rate_limit
    service_tier
    inference_geo
    model
    stop_reason
    stop_details
    usage
    thinking_tokens

Do not require every API to populate every field.

All fields should be optional unless guaranteed.

Validate:

non-stream Messages
streaming Messages
tool use
structured output
batch
token counting
error responses

where applicable.

============================================================
14. STREAMING METADATA
============================================================

Anthropic returns some usage metadata only in final streaming events.

Verify ZCoder does not finalize metrics before the final message delta.

Specifically inspect handling for:

usage
thinking_tokens
stop_reason
stop_details
request_id
workspace_id

Test:

1-token stream
short stream
multi-chunk stream
tool-call stream
refusal stream
connection interrupted before terminal event

Avoid double counting.

============================================================
15. REFUSAL BILLING CORRECTNESS
============================================================

Audit refusal handling.

Distinguish:

HTTP transport error

from:

HTTP 200
stop_reason = "refusal"

Ensure:

- no retry loop treats refusal as network failure
- fallback logic follows documented model rules
- pre-output refusals do not incorrectly accrue output cost
- streamed refusals finalize correctly
- stop_details are retained where available

Add regression tests.

============================================================
16. SONNET 5 TOKENIZER SAFETY
============================================================

Never estimate Sonnet 5 exact token counts by multiplying an older model
count by 1.3.

Audit for:

1.3
30%
token_factor
token_multiplier
estimated_tokens

Production decisions that require exact model token count should use the
Anthropic token counting API or actual response usage.

Estimated mode may exist only with explicit metadata:

exact = false
source = heuristic

============================================================
17. MODEL CAPABILITY AUTO-CONFORMANCE
============================================================

The Models API can expose supported capabilities/token limits.

Build a comparison layer:

LocalModelCapability
vs
RemoteModelCapability

Do not make local capability logic dependent on internet availability.

Command:

zcoder anthropic models diff

Example output:

MATCH
LOCAL_ONLY
REMOTE_ONLY
VALUE_CHANGED
POLICY_OVERRIDE

