============================================================
40. RELEASE-GATE MACHINE
============================================================

Implement a command such as:

zcoder release check

It should aggregate:

SOURCE_TRUTH
TESTS
BUILD
PACKAGE_INSTALL
VERSION
MODEL_REGISTRY
PRICING
DEPRECATIONS
CLI_WIRING
SECURITY
DOCS

Return non-zero if a required gate fails.

Example:

SOURCE_TRUTH_PASS=true
TEST_PASS=true
BUILD_PASS=true
PACKAGE_INSTALL_PASS=true
VERSION_PASS=true
MODEL_MATRIX_PASS=true
PRICING_PASS=true
CLI_WIRING_PASS=true

FINAL=PASS

Do not make this output decorative.
Its process exit status must reflect the result.

============================================================
41. MACHINE-READABLE RELEASE REPORT
============================================================

Support:

zcoder release check --json

Example:

{
  "version": "...",
  "result": "PASS",
  "tests": {
    "passed": ...,
    "failed": ...,
    "skipped": ...,
    "excluded": ...
  },
  "source_truth": {...},
  "build": {...},
  "security": {...}
}

Schema must be stable enough for CI.

============================================================
42. CI RELEASE GATE
============================================================

Create/update GitHub Actions.

Suggested logical jobs:

lint
typecheck
unit-tests
integration-tests
web-tests
tui-tests
package-build
wheel-install-smoke
security
anthropic-conformance-static
release-gate

Do not require Anthropic API credentials for pull-request CI.

Live Anthropic checks should be:

manual
scheduled
or protected environment

and read-only where possible.

============================================================
43. SCHEDULED ANTHROPIC DRIFT CHECK
============================================================

Create a scheduled CI workflow that can detect upstream drift.

It should NOT automatically modify main.

Instead generate an artifact/report when:

new release-note item
new model
retirement change
capability change
pricing manifest stale

If credentials are required, use repository/environment secrets.

Never print them.

============================================================
44. FAIL-SAFE SOURCE DRIFT
============================================================

A failed network fetch must result in:

UNKNOWN

not:

PASS

Distinguish:

NO_CHANGE
UPSTREAM_CHANGED
FETCH_FAILED
PARSE_FAILED
AUTH_FAILED

Never treat inability to verify as verification success.

============================================================
45. OPTIONAL LIVE CONTRACT TESTS
============================================================

Create an explicitly marked suite:

pytest -m anthropic_live

Requirements:

- disabled by default
- read-only/minimal-cost wherever possible
- never send sensitive repository content
- exact cost warning
- strong timeout
- no destructive Admin/Compliance writes

Use live tests for only behavior impossible to validate locally.

